# BlackEclipse line-ending normalization.
#
# WHY: `core.autocrlf=true` with no `.gitattributes` meant a one-line edit to a
# doc could show as a whole-file rewrite (CRLF vs LF), breaking `git blame` and
# review. This file normalizes text to LF in the repository so a real edit diffs
# as a real edit.
#
# The default: text files are stored LF-normalized and checked out LF. That is
# correct for this repo — its shell hooks (`.githooks/pre-commit`,
# `.githooks/commit-msg`) run under `sh`, where LF is required, and its Node/
# Python/TS tooling is line-ending agnostic.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only script types that must keep CRLF in the working tree, or they can
# fail to run. (Only `.ps1` is currently tracked; the others are declared so a
# future addition is safe rather than silently normalized.)
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Explicit text types (belt-and-braces over `text=auto`; keeps the intent clear).
*.md   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.mts  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg  text eol=lf

# Real binaries — never let git normalize or diff these as text. Determined from
# `git ls-files` + extension: `.wav` (63 tracked) and `.ico` (1 tracked) are the
# only binary types in the tree today. `.db` is listed so a future `jdds.db`-like
# file cannot be corrupted by a text normalization.
*.wav binary
*.ico binary
*.db  binary
*.db-* binary
